{
  "$schema": "./ui-merge-order-ceilings.schema.md",
  "contract": "UI_MERGE_ORDER = recipe -> ui -> class (@dzup-ui/contracts/composition, TASK-R5-O6 decision D38)",
  "sourceCommit": "99b963a",
  "measuredAt": "2026-09-15",
  "why": [
    "ADR-19 §5 defined the `ui` prop and said class and ui merge through the same cn(),",
    "but never said in which order. cn() is tailwind-merge, so the order IS the answer to",
    "\"which wins\". D38 ratifies recipe -> ui -> class: the consumer class is passed last and",
    "wins, which is what ADR-19 §5 promises (\"Nothing about existing usage changes\") and what",
    "keeps a wrapper's `ui` overridable without !important.",
    "The components below merge the other way. They are a recorded defect, NOT an exemption:",
    "the ceiling is downward-only, so the count can fall and can never rise, and a NEW",
    "component that merges the wrong way fails the contract lane immediately.",
    "They are not fixed here because re-ordering a merge changes rendered output, and",
    "TASK-R5-O6 writes the contract rather than migrating to it (task <stop_conditions>).",
    "Two idioms carry this merge: a cn() call, and a template array binding whose first",
    "element is a computed that already folded attrs.class in ([rootClasses, ui?.root]).",
    "The array form is 19 of the sites in 18 components and was invisible to the first",
    "version of this gate; the scanner reads both, and each entry records which."
  ],
  "maxDeviatingComponents": 73,
  "maxDeviatingSites": 74,
  "conformant": {
    "count": 5,
    "components": [
      "DzButton",
      "DzDialogContent",
      "DzInput",
      "DzSelect",
      "DzTable"
    ],
    "note": "Exactly the P3-03 pilot set in packages/core/stories/compositions/styling/Overrides.stories.ts, the fixture behind the only browser evidence the override contract has (e2e/components/styling-overrides.spec.ts). They are also the only five that merge in the ratified order — which is why D38 ratifies theirs and not the majority's."
  },
